        "date": "2026-11-08T08:09:19Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "austin62jake",
        "email": "340374338+austin62jake@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-08T08:09:19Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app): the program sim sweeps a tap at its thread's minor diameter\n\nThe program sim (the post gate's stock-sim clause) swept a Tap-kind tool\nat its full major diameter. CAD models a tapped hole at the thread's\nminor (tap-drill) size, and the tap only cuts the thread band outside\nthat wall, so the sim read the band as a gouge down the whole hole wall\nand refused the post (a 12 mm \"gouge\" for an M6 tap in a 5 mm hole).\n\nA Tap-kind tool now sweeps its thread's core, d/2 - 0.5413 x pitch (ISO\n724, the depth the thread-mill generator already uses), through one\nshared rule, operation::tool_law::cutting_radius. Every other tool\nstill sweeps half its diameter. A tap over a hole smaller than its core\nstill gouges, and a pitch that leaves no core is refused by name.\n\nPartial: the tap op's own verify still judges the tap at its full\ndiameter, so the post stays blocked by its two \"cuts past the finish\nsurface\" warnings. That half is left for the maintainer to decide on\nthe issue (docs/decisions/266-tap-minor-sweep.md).\n\nRefs #266\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
